# Generated / machine-specific build artifacts — never committed (the
# `tauri-plugin-qr-scan` `.gitignore` discipline; the gradle module keeps its
# own `android/.gitignore`, matching screen-guard / share-intent).
# `.tauri/` is the generated Tauri-API surface; `ios/.build/` holds SwiftPM +
# SourceKit index output (incl. binary `*.mdb`); `Package.resolved` re-resolves
# from the local `../.tauri/tauri-api` path at each build.
/.tauri
/ios/.build
/ios/Package.resolved
# Created by an ISOLATED Swift compile of this package, which is worth doing and
# is recorded in the feature's progress notes:
#   cd ios && xcodebuild build -scheme tauri-plugin-reminders \
#     -destination 'generic/platform=iOS' -derivedDataPath <scratch>
# It needs `../.tauri/tauri-api` to exist, which any `cargo check` of this crate
# materializes. That is the only way the Swift half gets a compiler at all
# without a full `tauri ios build`.
/ios/.swiftpm
